    <h2>What your browser asks you</h2>
    <p>Nothing happens until you've done both of these yourself:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><b>Give it the log.</b> You drag <code>UE_game.log</code> from the game's log folder in File Explorer onto this page, or choose it in the browser's file window (step 1 at the top lists the folders). Either way, the site gets read-only access to that one file and nothing else. The file window refuses files under Program Files, where Steam puts games by default; dragging works anywhere (or <a href="steam-library.html">move the game</a>). On your next visit, the browser asks again before the site can read it.</li>
      <li><b>To share a window.</b> The browser lists your open windows, and you pick Torchlight: Infinite. Whole screens aren't offered. While the window is shared, the browser shows which one, with a button to stop.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Browsers never tell a website which program a window belongs to: not its name, its title or its process. So the code can't check that the window is the game. What it does check is that you shared one window, not your screen or a browser tab, and the browser's sharing bar shows you which window that is. Pick the game, and only the game is seen.</p>
    <p class="note">Other browsers can't follow a file on your PC, so Auto Screenshot Mode needs Chrome or Edge on a PC. Run the game borderless or windowed: in exclusive fullscreen, a shared window looks black.</p>
====
    <h2>瀏覽器會問你什麼</h2>
    <p>在你親自完成下面兩件事之前，什麼都不會發生：</p>
    <ol>
      <li><b>交出紀錄檔。</b>你從檔案總管裡遊戲的紀錄檔資料夾把 <code>UE_game.log</code> 拖到這個頁面，或在瀏覽器的檔案視窗中選擇它（最上方的步驟 1 列出了資料夾位置）。無論哪種方式，網站都只能唯讀存取那一個檔案，其他什麼都不行。檔案視窗會拒絕 Program Files 底下的檔案，而 Steam 預設就把遊戲裝在那裡；用拖曳的在哪裡都行（或<a href="steam-library.html">把遊戲移走</a>）。下次造訪時，瀏覽器會先再問你一次，網站才能讀取。</li>
