    <h3>3. It reads only the new lines</h3>
    <p>Once a second, the follower checks whether the log has grown, and reads only the part added since its last look. It starts at the end of the log, so nothing written before you connected is ever read. Each new line is checked against the triggers below. A line that matches nothing is dropped; a line that matches the watch pattern is shown to you on the page. It runs in a background worker, so it keeps up when the tab is hidden. However the log changes, each look reads at most the newest megabyte and passes at most 200 lines to the page, so the page never has more than it can handle. If the log is deleted, the follower waits, and reads the next log the game writes from its start. The game also writes its language in the log every few minutes (a line with <code>sdkLang=…</code>). The follower notes only that language code, so the analyzer can tell you when names and labels may not be read. Nothing else from that line is kept, shown or sent.</p>
