    <h3>7. The analyzer reads it into your board</h3>
    <p>The analyzer answers only after you've agreed, and reads only the pictures sent to it. The screenshot reader, running in your browser, turns the picture into a board, which becomes your board straight away, and the analyzer gives its advice. Cells the reader is unsure of are marked Check. If anything doesn't match your game, fix it on the board and press Recheck. A picture of the objective popup sets the run's objective, read from its title. A picture of the instrument pick is read as that instead: the analyzer starts a fresh run at the offer, with the three instruments it read and whether a re-roll is left, and says which to take, or to re-roll. The instruments are read by their printed names first, with an OCR engine (Tesseract) that the analyzer downloads once from jsDelivr, a public code host, and runs in your browser: the picture itself isn’t sent anywhere. Where a name isn’t clear, the card’s art is used. An instrument it's unsure of is named for you to check. Only how the reading went goes back to this page. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
