    <p>You don't drag the log in. The app looks where the game writes it. While the game runs, that's beside the game itself: Windows tells the app two things about the game: where its program file is, and whether the game (or the program that started it) runs as administrator. The second goes only into the app's debug log, because Windows cuts off a window share to an app that doesn't run as administrator too. The app learns nothing else about it. Otherwise it looks in each Steam library that has the game (from Steam's own list of its libraries) and in the game launcher's default folder, and takes the newest <code>UE_game.log</code> there. You can also choose a log from its tray menu, drag one onto this page, or use the button in step 1. In the app, the app itself reads that file, so it works wherever the game is installed and doesn't ask again. Only this page can read it, and only its size and the bytes it asks for. The follower above still reads only the new lines.</p>
